{"id":"e14t3","name":"Daily Store Sales Calendar","lang":"sql","entry":null,"params":[],"limit_s":10,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>The operations team builds a dashboard that plots daily sales per store. The chart must show every day of the reporting period for every store, including the days without any sale.</p>\n<h3>Tables</h3>\n<p><code>stores</code></p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>column</th>\n<th>type</th>\n<th>description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>store_id</td>\n<td>INT</td>\n<td>primary key</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>store_name</td>\n<td>VARCHAR(50)</td>\n<td>not null</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><code>sales</code></p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>column</th>\n<th>type</th>\n<th>description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>sale_id</td>\n<td>INT</td>\n<td>primary key</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>store_id</td>\n<td>INT</td>\n<td>not null; may reference a store that does not exist in <code>stores</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>sale_ts</td>\n<td>TIMESTAMP</td>\n<td>not null, date and time of the sale</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>amount</td>\n<td>DECIMAL(10,2)</td>\n<td>not null, strictly positive</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>status</td>\n<td>VARCHAR(20)</td>\n<td>not null, one of <code>'completed'</code>, <code>'pending'</code>, <code>'refunded'</code>, <code>'cancelled'</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h3>Rules</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>A valid sale has status <code>'completed'</code> and a <code>store_id</code> that exists in <code>stores</code>. Other sales are ignored everywhere, including in rule 2.</li>\n<li>The reporting period goes from the date of the earliest valid sale to the date of the latest valid sale, both inclusive. The date of a sale is the calendar date of <code>sale_ts</code>.</li>\n<li>Return one row for every store of <code>stores</code> and every day of the reporting period, even if the store has no sale that day.</li>\n<li><code>num_sales</code> is the number of valid sales of the store on that day, and <code>revenue</code> is the sum of their amounts; both are 0 when there is no sale.</li>\n<li>If there is no valid sale at all, return no rows.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Output</h3>\n<p>Exactly these columns, in this order:</p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>column</th>\n<th>type</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>store_id</td>\n<td>INT</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>sale_date</td>\n<td>DATE</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>num_sales</td>\n<td>INT (or BIGINT)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>revenue</td>\n<td>DECIMAL, 2 decimals</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Rows are sorted by <code>store_id</code> ascending, then <code>sale_date</code> ascending.</p>\n<h3>Example</h3>\n<p><code>stores</code></p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>store_id</th>\n<th>store_name</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>Maarif</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>Gauthier</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>Agdal</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><code>sales</code></p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>sale_id</th>\n<th>store_id</th>\n<th>sale_ts</th>\n<th>amount</th>\n<th>status</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>2024-03-01 09:15:00</td>\n<td>100.00</td>\n<td>completed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>2024-03-01 23:59:59</td>\n<td>50.00</td>\n<td>completed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>2024-03-02 10:00:00</td>\n<td>80.00</td>\n<td>refunded</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>2024-03-03 00:00:00</td>\n<td>40.00</td>\n<td>completed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>9</td>\n<td>2024-02-28 12:00:00</td>\n<td>70.00</td>\n<td>completed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>2024-03-04 08:30:00</td>\n<td>25.50</td>\n<td>cancelled</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Expected output</p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>store_id</th>\n<th>sale_date</th>\n<th>num_sales</th>\n<th>revenue</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>2024-03-01</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>150.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>2024-03-02</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>2024-03-03</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>2024-03-01</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>2024-03-02</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>2024-03-03</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>40.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>2024-03-01</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>2024-03-02</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>2024-03-03</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0.00</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h3>Constraints</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Dialect: PostgreSQL.</li>\n<li>Write a single <code>SELECT</code> statement (CTEs allowed, including recursive CTEs). Do not create tables or views.</li>\n<li><code>stores</code> has up to 500 rows, <code>sales</code> up to 10^6 rows, and the reporting period is at most 366 days.</li>\n</ul><p class=\"muted\">Write a PostgreSQL query.</p><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 10 seconds (psql)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB</div>","starter":"/* Write your PostgreSQL query here */\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":[],"minutes":22,"source":"Examen d'entraînement d'octobre n°6, question 3","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"tables":{"stores":{"columns":[["store_id","INT"],["store_name","VARCHAR(50)"]],"rows":[[1,"Maarif"],[2,"Gauthier"],[3,"Agdal"]]},"sales":{"columns":[["sale_id","INT"],["store_id","INT"],["sale_ts","TIMESTAMP"],["amount","NUMERIC(10,2)"],["status","VARCHAR(20)"]],"rows":[[1,1,"2024-03-01 09:15:00","100.00","completed"],[2,1,"2024-03-01 23:59:59","50.00","completed"],[3,2,"2024-03-02 10:00:00","80.00","refunded"],[4,2,"2024-03-03 00:00:00","40.00","completed"],[5,9,"2024-02-28 12:00:00","70.00","completed"],[6,2,"2024-03-04 08:30:00","25.50","cancelled"]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["store_id","sale_date","num_sales","revenue"],"rows":[[1,"2024-03-01",2,150.0],[1,"2024-03-02",0,0.0],[1,"2024-03-03",0,0.0],[2,"2024-03-01",0,0.0],[2,"2024-03-02",0,0.0],[2,"2024-03-03",1,40.0],[3,"2024-03-01",0,0.0],[3,"2024-03-02",0,0.0],[3,"2024-03-03",0,0.0]]}}],"hidden_n":4,"hidden":"","solution":""}